  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far (config_019, acc=0.542) uses scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. Across experiments, avgpool consistently beats transformer, imagenet_vit_l beats resnet50, and weighted beats concat. However, scgpt is the only RNA encoder tested, leaving a major design dimension unexplored. Question: Can scvi_n200 (a learned 200-dim VAE embedding) match or exceed scgpt when paired with the best-known image/aggregation/fusion settings? config_026 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap from config_019, isolating the RNA encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: With 5 experiments remaining, identifying whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck or whether scgpt is near-optimal is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. If scvi_n200 matches scgpt, we gain a cheaper encoder; if it falls short, we confirm scgpt's importance and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning other axes. Expected cost: ~5–7 GPU hours (scvi_n200 is lighter than scgpt, imagenet_vit_l dominates, avgpool is cheap), comparable to or slightly below config_035's 7.18 h."
}

